### Limitations the authors admit
- 2019ApJ...881...10B: Model not a formally acceptable fit (chi^2_nu=1.179); correlated noise; local irregularities in velocity/dispersion fields
- 2019ApJ...881...10B: Distance disagreements among estimates imply M_BH may lie in (2.0-3.8)e9 Msun
- 2024ApJ...975..179C: Relatively low S/N; chi2_nu underestimated because adjacent down-sampled pixels not independent
- 2024ApJ...975..179C: Systematic uncertainty in gas mass likely underestimated
- 2017ApJ...843L..35W: ~50% of data flagged due to antenna problems
- 2017ApJ...843L..35W: Conjugate points cause degeneracies; position uncertainties overestimated
- 2019ApJ...883..193N: Missing flux from lack of short baselines, so masses are lower limits
- 2019ApJ...883..193N: Residual is not a true chi2 because neighbouring pixels are correlated; modelling assumptions simple
- 2015ApJ...811..115W: Fluxes of A, B, C not used owing to differential magnification (~30-50%)
- 2020MNRAS.496.4061D: Keplerian rise not resolved; result depends on stellar mass model and Gamma
- 2020MNRAS.496.4061D: Low Gamma should be treated with caution; beam correlations neglected
- 2020A&AT...31..423B: Work in progress
- 2025A&A...700A.285W: Torque method unvalidated by simulations, configuration likely unstable
- 2025A&A...700A.285W: Mass of young component is poorly constrained from single UV band; closed-box and alpha_CO assumptions
- 2020A&A...637A..84P: Poor angular resolution prevents constraining Mdyn for most; thin-disc assumption too simple for some perturbed systems; MBH systematics up to ~0.4 dex
- 2013ApJ...768L..38H: Beam too large to measure brightness temperature or resolve kinematics
- 2018MNRAS.473.3818D: Central gas hole makes SMBH mass sensitive to stellar mass modelling
- 2025MNRAS.541.2540Z: Circular-orbit assumption with mild non-circular motions; distance uncertainty (10%) not included in budget
- 2016ApJ...816...37V: Inclination and peak rotation velocity cannot be independently determined at current resolution
- 2016ApJ...816...37V: FIR/TIR luminosities strongly model dependent; more photometry needed
- 2017ApJ...849...91M: High-z sample biased to high luminosities
- 2013ApJ...770...13W: Source only marginally resolved; intrinsic size poorly constrained and inclination unknown
- 2013ApJ...770...13W: L_FIR uncertainties exclude dust temperature uncertainty
- 2020ApJ...892...68N: Tilted-ring uncertainties likely underestimated; distance systematics large
- 2020ApJ...897L..14Y: Black hole mass uncertainty excludes scaling-relation systematics of up to ~0.5 dex
- 2020ApJ...897L..14Y: Large uncertainties and a broad PDF for x_HI prevent solid conclusions
- 2024PASJ...76..340K: Red component decomposition not unique; drift versus growth ambiguous; first epoch had poorer uv coverage
- 2019A&A...621A..83S: Distance uncertain; warped or non-coplanar disks cannot be constrained; outer CO velocity field sparse
- 2025ApJ...992..211N: Distance uncertainty (69.3 vs 46.4 Mpc) gives ~30% systematic in MBH, dominant error
- 2017ApJ...845..138S: Inclination derived from only two successful rings; real uncertainty may be much larger
- 2019ApJ...887...74F: Limited depth and resolution prevent distinguishing disk, merger and outflow
- 2019ApJ...887...74F: Dust mass depends strongly on the adopted kappa
- 2015PASJ...67...72T: Core radius and velocity dispersion highly degenerate; BH mass and core radius degenerate
- 2020ApJ...898...75I: Dominance of H2 in the CND is assumed; HI/HII may contribute
- 2020ApJ...898...75I: RADEX assumes single homogeneous medium though real structure is complex; single transition limits Tex
- 2020ApJ...891...64F: Lens model poorly constrained; magnification uncertain by a factor of a few
- 2016ApJ...827...81I: Small, inhomogeneous samples; tentative results; fixed eta and uncertainties not fully included
- 2016ApJ...827...81I: Most CNDs unresolved so Sigma_dense not measured
- 2025A&A...693A.311P: One network per galaxy; simulations lack bars, clumps and misalignments; uncertainties not physical
- 2018PASJ...70...36I: Mdyn has large unconstrained systematic uncertainty; sources only marginally resolved
- 2018A&A...617A..82B: Inclinations and sizes of marginally resolved sources are uncertain, affecting dynamical masses
- 2016ApJ...823...51B: Models are poor fits (chi2_nu 4.4); warp, sigma_turb and surface brightness models inadequate; no meaningful confidence intervals
- 2024MNRAS.527.9343L: Fluxes and masses for NGC 1194 and NGC 3393 are lower limits due to FoV; uncertainties exclude systematics
- 2024MNRAS.527.9343L: Spectral indices may be biased since resolution not matched to VLA
- 2018ApJ...854...97D: Low angular resolution means sizes are tentative and dynamical masses may be overestimated
- 2019ApJ...879..117K: Small LEQ sample; quasars not a complete sample
- 2019ApJ...879..117K: Alternative explanations (episodic super-Eddington accretion) possible
- 2019ApJ...872...69P: Fundamental plane is a rough jet estimator; large ALMA beams may overestimate fluxes
- 2024ApJ...977..238B: Original-resolution cube has insufficient per-pixel emission; detection only after rebinning to 12.9 km/s

