### 2016ApJ...823...51B: Toward Precision Black Hole Masses with ALMA: NGC 1332 as a Case Study in Molecular Disk Dynamics (2016; nearby_galaxies, agn_and_quasars; observational_alma_primary)
- question: Can ALMA CO(2-1) kinematics of the NGC 1332 circumnuclear disk, at 0.3'' resolution, constrain the central black hole mass, and what limits the measurement?
- step 5: Fit models to data cube
  - method: chi^2 minimization with amoeba on 4x4 block-averaged cube; 49 pixels x 52 channels = 2548 data points; grids over fixed M_BH [4.4 Model Optimization: "We fit models using the `amoeba` downhill simplex method implemented in IDL."]
  - software: IDL amoeba
  - parameter: Free: M_BH, Upsilon, x, y, v_sys, i, Gamma, f0, sigma_turb params [4.1 Method: "Free parameters in the model include $M_\mathrm{BH}$ and $\Upsilon$, the $x$ and $y$ centroid positions of the BH, the systemic velocity $v_\mathrm{sys}$"]
  - fitting: chi^2 with noise from block-averaged blank regions (0.3 mJy/beam); covariance matrix attempt failed [4.4 Model Optimization: "The RMS noise level in the $4\times4$ block-averaged data is 0.3 mJy beam$^{-1}$"]
  - validation: Compared full-resolution chi^2, PVD fits, HST mass profile [5.1 Initial tests: "the results for the best-fitting parameters were virtually identical to the block-averaged fits"]
- result: Best flat-sigma M_BH = 6.02e8 ± not meaningful (chi2_nu=4.40) Msun [5.2 Model fits with flat sigma_turb: "The best-fitting model with flat $\sigma_\mathrm{turb}$ is found at $\ensuremath{M_\mathrm{BH}}= 6.02\times10^8$ ${M}_{\odot}$."]
- result: Best-fit flat sigma_turb = 24.7 ± not stated km/s [5.2 Model fits with flat sigma_turb: "$\Upsilon_R = 7.25$ and $\ensuremath{\sigma_\mathrm{turb}}= 24.7$ km s$^{-1}$"]
- result: Disk inclination = 83-84 ± not stated deg [5.2 Model fits with flat sigma_turb: "inclination $i = 83\ensuremath{^\circ}-84\ensuremath{^\circ}$"]
- result: Systemic velocity = 1559 ± ±1 km/s [5.2 Model fits with flat sigma_turb: "$\ensuremath{v_\mathrm{sys}}= 1559\pm1$ km s$^{-1}$"]
- result: Provisional BH mass range = ~(4-8)e8 ± not rigorous Msun [5.5 Final Results: "point to a BH mass that is likely to be in the range $\sim(4-8)\times10^8$ ${M}_{\odot}$"]
- result: BH mass with sigma_turb=10 km/s = 8.0e8 ± not stated Msun [5.2 Model fits with flat sigma_turb: "For $\ensuremath{\sigma_\mathrm{turb}}=10$ km s$^{-1}$, the best-fitting BH mass is $8.0\times10^8$ ${M}_{\odot}$."]
- result: Gaussian sigma_turb model chi2 (M_BH=0) = 7499.7 for 2538 dof ± not stated dimensionless [5.3 Model fits with other sigma_turb pr…: "the best-fitting $\chi^2$ value in this case is 7499.7 for 2538 degrees of freedom"]
- limitation (authors): Models are poor fits (chi2_nu 4.4); warp, sigma_turb and surface brightness models inadequate; no meaningful confidence intervals [5.5 Final Results: "We are unable to derive meaningful confidence limits on $M_\mathrm{BH}$"]
